# CEP:FILE: .gitignore
# CEP:WHAT: Build-artifact hygiene: Rocq kernel outputs and Rust build caches are regenerable evidence, not source; the sources and the recorded artifacts (tools/fv/) are the evidence chain.
# CEP:WHY: Keeps git status to real changes; the .vo files are reproducible by rocq/build.sh, the target/ dirs by cargo.
# CEP:STATUS: complete
# CEP:FAILURE: A tracked build artifact would rot against its source; untracked source would be a missing evidence link.
# CEP:ASSUMES: rocq/build.sh and cargo regenerate everything ignored here.
# CEP:COST: none.
# CEP:EVIDENCE: rocq/build.sh; cargo.
# CEP:SECURITY: repository-trusted inputs.
*.vo
*.vok
*.vos
*.glob
.*.aux
target/
rocq/.lia.cache
*.long-type-*.txt
